// A generic instance's METHOD renders with its type arguments, not with the argument mangle.
//
// `demangleForDisplay` looks a token up in `_genericTypeInsts`, which is keyed by the instance mangle
// ALONE. A method symbol is `<instance>__<method>`, so it missed, fell past the scope strips, and came
// out of the `__`-to-`::` fallback still carrying the mangle: this chain read
// `std::collections::DynamicArray_string_kama::GlobalAllocator::dtor`. Every reader of a no-heap chain
// saw that, and it is also the exact shape of every debugger frame inside a generic (KR-32).
//
// `string` rather than `int32` as the argument so the rendering has something to get wrong, and the
// allocator left at its default so the trailing-default drop is asserted too — the mangle expands
// `GlobalAllocator` positionally, and a demangler that did not drop it would say
// `DynamicArray<string, GlobalAllocator>::dtor`.
import { std::collections::DynamicArray };
@noheap fn int32 tick(int32 n) {
    DynamicArray<string> l = DynamicArray.empty();
    return n;
}
fn int32 main() { return tick(n: 7); }
